          <p>
            Multipacks change the picture more than brand does. PUR and Brita both sell cartridges in two-, three-, four- and six-packs on Amazon, and the per-cartridge price drops sharply in the larger packs. Third-party replacements for PUR cartridges are also everywhere; Waterdrop sells one. They may fit, but they do not inherit PUR's certification, so check whether the replacement has its own listed certification to NSF/ANSI 53 before trusting it with lead.
