          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If your kitchen faucet has a fixed spout and a removable aerator, buy the PUR PLUS PFM400H. Its cartridge has the broadest published certification of any faucet filter we could find, covering lead, total PFAS and microplastics, and the filtered water costs about what a pitcher's does. Pick the vertical FM-3700 instead if the horizontal body crowds your sink, and the Brita Elite if you prefer its spray options and are not worried about PFAS.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If your faucet is a pull-down sprayer, do not buy any of these. Go under the sink or onto the countertop. And whatever you buy, check the standard behind the claim: NSF/ANSI 53 for lead and PFAS, not 42 or 372 dressed up as something more.
          </p>
